[moxley@ccwf.cc.utexas.edu (Richard Moxley) writes:]
[] I have Mac NetHack 3.0i patch level 9.  How do I get it to play a game in
[] Wizard mode?

the directions for entering wizard-mode are outlined in the NH3.09.doc
(available at linc.cis.upenn.edu, pub/NH3.0/mac) which should accompany
the game.

the trick (it's a bit awkward) is to start a normal game, set the default
name in the options menu to "wizard", quit that game and then restart.
the dialog box will now be visible since your default name is "wizard"
(note the spelling).  change the default name again to disable this
feature.

future versions of mac nethack should have an easier method for accessing
wizard-mode.

btw, linc.cis.upenn.edu also has pl9 source and IBM-PC, OS/2, amiga and
atari binaries in appropriate sub-directories.  the source supports the
above-mentioned platforms, UNIX (obviously) and VMS.

